guideline(0, "The name of a measured variable or characteristic, possibly with its unit or the statistic reported for it, such as 'Age, years', 'Chronic kidney disease', 'HDL-C (mmol/L)' or 'Silt (%)'", 'VariableLabel').
guideline(1, "A unit of measurement on its own, such as 'mg/dL' or 'per 1000 person years'", 'Unit').
guideline(2, "The name of a statistic or measure, as used in a heading, such as 'Risk Ratio (Random, 95% CI)', 'p value', 'Aetiology, No. (%)' or 'Cumulative Variance (%)'", 'StatisticLabel').
guideline(3, "The title of a section or block of a table, which groups the rows or columns under it rather than describing one of them, such as 'Secondary outcomes', 'Classification metrics' or 'Block 2 Occupation-specific variables'", 'SectionLabel').
guideline(4, "A question or criterion of an appraisal or reporting checklist, or of a domain such as risk of bias, such as 'Was a list of studies (included and excluded) provided?' or 'Blinding of outcome assessment (detection bias) All outcomes'", 'ChecklistItem').
guideline(5, "A level of a categorical variable, or the name of a group, arm, time point or condition being compared, such as 'Male', 'College or above', 'Never', 'At sowing', 'Placebo' or '0–15 cm'", 'CategoryLevel').
guideline(6, "A rating on a fixed scale, as given in quality, risk of bias or certainty assessments, such as 'Low', 'Unclear', 'Partial yes', 'High risk' or '⊕⊕⊝⊝ LOW'", 'QualityJudgment').
guideline(7, "The name of an individual entity that a row or column describes: a study or trial, a drug, chemical or material, a gene or protein, a species, a sample, site, region or brain area, such as 'Tirlazad', 'ZRSR2', 'Bromus inermis Leyss.', 'Korea' or 'Putamen'", 'EntityName').
guideline(8, "A description of how a study was done or who it covered: design, setting, population, eligibility criteria, or search strategy, such as 'Double blind randomized controlled trial', 'Cluster‐RCT Unit of randomization: household', 'Patients >18 years old with HD duration of at least 3 months' or 'Diagnos* OR detect* OR screen*'", 'StudyCharacteristic').
guideline(9, "A description of what was given or done to the participants or samples, such as 'HC bolus 200 mg, followed by an infusion rate of 10 mg/h for 7 days' or 'Mosquito coils (0.03% transfluthrin) and no treatment'", 'InterventionDescription').
guideline(10, "A statement in words of what a study found or concluded, such as 'Decreased amplitude responses in the left insula.' or 'Screening with health promotion may have little or no effect on mortality.'", 'FindingStatement').
guideline(11, "A reason, quotation, comment or limitation that supports or qualifies an assessment, such as 'Comment: Not described, but usually low risk in cluster‐randomized trials' or 'Only data from the intervention areas are presented.'", 'JudgmentRationale').
guideline(12, "A description of a person's subjective experience", 'PhenomenologicalData').
